hi this is presh talwalkar in this video  i'm going to explain the solution to the  15 puzzle from last week but before i  get into that i want to explain three  clues  if you compare the original version of  the puzzle to the version we used the  version we used had round discs instead  of square blocks  the second clue is if you looked at the  transition between the puzzle  and its solution  the transition was a rotation transition  the third clue  is that i cut out  the 4x4 grid  which seemingly served no purpose at all  the reason was if you compared the  original configuration to the solved  puzzle  and you looked very closely you could  see  that the grid was actually rotated in  the solved puzzle from where it was  originally  all right let's get to the solution  we'll start by sliding  the disks around the perimeter of the  grid  the reason is that we want to get the  numbers 1 2 3 and 4  to be vertically on the right hand side  so keep sliding the numbers around  until you get two to be in the upper  right hand corner  at this point move the second column  slide that entire second column up  and this is because we want to exchange  the 14 in a different position  now we keep sliding the discs around the  perimeter  until we get one two three and four on  the right hand side  after we do this for a little while we  now very importantly need to move the 14  in between the 13 and 15 the 11 in  between the 10 and 12  and with the few obvious moves  we'll be able to get all of the numbers  in order  in columns on the right hand side  now comes the trick we rotate the entire  board 90 degrees counterclockwise  and then we rotate each of the discs 90  degrees clockwise  and once we do that  we will have solved the puzzle and put  the numbers in order 1 through 15 by  sliding the discs around  inside the grid  basically thinking inside the box  i hope you like this video please  subscribe to my channel  you can get my books listed on my  website catch me on my blog